        "geology": "Wet Meadows located in the T?ebo? basin which is a small depression in the southern part of Bohemian Massif. It is cretaceous basin represented by cenomanian fine sandstones and clay, turonian marls and sandstones and senonian fine sandstones and clay. The thickness of sediment is shallow with a maxima of 150m.",
        "hydrology": "The Wet Meadows is situated in the inundation area of a large human-made lake (Ro?mberk fishpond, 5 km2). The water level is controlled by a system of ditches, which interconnect the man-made lakes (fishponds) in the whole region, and is thus fairly stable throughout the year. In some years, however, spring or summer floods occur as a consequence of snow melting or summer rains, respectively. Extreme floods occurred in summer 2002, 2013 and spring 2006, when water level at the site culminated at 2 m above the soil surface.",
        "soils": "Prevailing soil on the Wet Meadows is organic soils, developed on deposits of peat.",
        "vegetation": "The vegetation of the Wet Meadows is formed mainly by dominant tall sedges (Carex acuta, Carex vesicaria) and hygrophytic grasses (especially Calamagrostis canescens)."
      },
